  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is the locus of a point, which moves such that it is always equidistant from the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi></math> equals",
    "image": null
  },
